      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Certification Checklist",
      "Anchor": "certification-checklist",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "All Verified Plus partners must complete this certification process to be approved for production access. The checklist covers OAuth integration, verification workflows, error handling, and LinkedIn policy compliance.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Certification Checklist",
      "Anchor": "certification-checklist",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "You must demonstrate and document completion of each requirement with screenshots, logs, or product flow explanations as appropriate.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Certification Areas",
      "Anchor": "certification-areas",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Certification Areas"
      ],
      "Text": "The checklist is divided into the following four categories:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "table",
      "Section": "Integration Requirements",
      "Anchor": "integration-requirements",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Requirements"
      ],
      "Text": "",
      "Headers": [
        "ID",
        "Requirement",
        "Expectations"
      ],
      "Rows": [
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-001",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "OAuth 2.0 Integration with Correct Scopes",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Implement OAuth 2.0 using the appropriate scopes for your use case. Only request the scopes that are required, such as: r_profile_basicinfo, r_most_recent_education, r_primary_current_experience, and r_verify_details. Requesting additional scopes may result in unnecessarily large responses or data beyond the partner\u2019s intended use case, leading to integration mismatches or unused information.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-002",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Latest API Endpoint and Version Compliance",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Confirm that your integration uses the latest recommended endpoints (/identityMe, /verificationReport, /validationStatus), does not use deprecated APIs, and includes the LinkedIn-Version header with the latest supported version in all requests. See Current API Versions for the latest versions.",
            "Links": [
              "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/linkedin/consumer/integrations/verified-on-linkedin/release-notes#current-api-versions"
            ],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-003",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Token Expiration \u0026 Management",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Reuse valid access tokens when available. If the access token has expired, use the refresh token to obtain a new one. If the refresh token is also expired or invalid, re-trigger the OAuth flow with the member to obtain a new access token.",
            "Links": [
              "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/linkedin/shared/authentication/programmatic-refresh-tokens"
            ],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-004",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Breaking Change Policy",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Confirm that you have read and agreed to LinkedIn\u2019s breaking change policy.",
            "Links": [
              "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/linkedin/shared/breaking-change-policy"
            ],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-005",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Handle API Errors such as Version Expiry \u0026 Rate Limiting",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Capture version expiry errors, monitor 426 responses, track X-LI-UUID, include the LinkedIn-Version header in all requests, monitor relevant HTTP errors, handle rate limiting correctly, and comply with LinkedIn\u2019s query tunneling and versioning policies.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "Kind": "table",
      "Section": "Verification Workflow",
      "Anchor": "verification-workflow",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Verification Workflow"
      ],
      "Text": "",
      "Headers": [
        "ID",
        "Requirement",
        "Expectations"
      ],
      "Rows": [
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-006",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Show Complete Verification Flow (New User)",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Demonstrate full flow: user clicks the \u0022Verify on LinkedIn\u0022 CTA \u2192 redirected to LinkedIn \u2192 completes verification \u2192 redirected back \u2192 display verified badge with category (Identity, Workplace) and timestamp.",
            "Links": [
              "https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/a1631613"
            ],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-007",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Verification Badge Implementation",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Use \u201CVerified on LinkedIn\u201D text, proper LinkedIn branding, link badge to the member\u2019s LinkedIn profile, and display verification category and timestamp.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-008",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Fetch Basic Member Profile via /identityMe",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Retrieve and use basic member information from /identityMe and explain how it is used in your platform.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-009",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Verification Flow for Pre-Verified Users",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Demonstrate flows for users with identity only, workplace only, both, and multiple verifications. Show ability to request specific verification types based on use case.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-010",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Handle Incomplete or Cancelled Verification Flow",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Handle user cancellations, consent rejection, and OAuth revocation. Ensure proper redirection and clear error messaging.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-011",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Error Logging \u0026 UUID Tracking",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Demonstrate error handling with request/response logs including headers, especially X-LI-UUID.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "Kind": "table",
      "Section": "Data Freshness",
      "Anchor": "data-freshness",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Data Freshness"
      ],
      "Text": "",
      "Headers": [
        "ID",
        "Requirement",
        "Expectations"
      ],
      "Rows": [
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-012",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Persist Critical Fields for Data Freshness",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Store id from /identityMe and /verificationReport, securely store refresh_token, and track lastRefreshedAt to avoid processing stale updates.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-013",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Validation Status API Polling Workflow",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Implement 2-legged OAuth with r_validation_status, call /validationStatus with up to 500 member IDs per request, handle VALID, INVALID, VALID_WITH_UPDATES, and refresh data using /verificationReport and /identityMe only when needed.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-014",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Push Notifications Handling (if subscribed)",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Register webhook endpoint, handle FEDERATED_MEMBER_DATA_STATUS_CHANGE, process isAccessRevoked, use timestamps to avoid duplicate or out-of-order events, and ensure webhook delivery health.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "Text": "SL-015",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Handle Access Revocation",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          },
          {
            "Text": "Delete or invalidate stored data and tokens when access is revoked and ensure proper user experience with clear error messaging.",
            "Links": [],
            "Values": []
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "Kind": "table",
      "Section": "Integration Compliance",
      "Anchor": "integration-compliance",
      "SectionPath": [
